WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:11.440
Well, my biggest hope is in fact that
there is a future to the Arctic.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:18.520
As it looks now we are changing the Arctic 
in such a fundamental way that perhaps

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:27.140
what we once considered the Arctic; as a far removed place that it would be difficult to get to is changing.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:34.160
The Arctic may in fact become a very easy and accessible place to go to. But then it would no longer be

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:41.280
the Arctic - it actually would be a melting Arctic - and it would change fundamentally the way we look

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:48.000
at the world, and the way the world would appear to us because the temperature of the world would rise

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.180
so much that the whole structure and infrastructure and ecosystem of the world would change.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.040
I often say that when I think about the word 'future' 
I think about the poet

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.260
- the 20th century French poet Paul Valéry -

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:08.000
who said: "The future isn't what it used
to be" and it strikes me that the future

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:14.560
of the Arctic is in our hands and we can
probably reverse the way in which the

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:20.820
Arctic is being destroyed by being
actively engaged in social change.

